tring)'.\"\n./forge/tests/test_forge_metadata.py-385-                    ),\n./forge/tests/test_forge_metadata.py-386-                ) as issue_body, \\\n./forge/tests/test_forge_metadata.py-387-                patch.object(\n./forge/tests/test_forge_metadata.py-388-                    forge_metadata,\n./forge/tests/test_forge_metadata.py-389-                    \"select_library_update_route\",\n--\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-47-   `PASSED`.\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-48-3. If native testing still fails after JVM-agent metadata was generated, or if\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-49-   the JVM-agent metadata path failed, use native tracing as a fallback. Each\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-50-   fallback cycle invokes\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-51-   `./gradlew runNativeTraceImage`; the trace binary is built with\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-52-   `-H:+MetadataTracingSupport`, `--exact-reachability-metadata`, and\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md:53:   `-H:MissingRegistrationReportingMode=Exit`.\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-54-4. If native tracing converges, merge the accepted trace dirs into\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-55-   `<output_dir>/trace`, then run one final native-image-utils merge over\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-56-   existing durable metadata, `<output_dir>/agent` when present, and\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-57-   `<output_dir>/trace` when present. The final merge result is copied to\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-58-   `metadata/<group>/<artifact>/<version>/reachability-metadata.json`, and\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-59-   the gate returns `PASSED`. If tracing stalls, exhausts its budget, or\n--\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-78-\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-79-The gate closes those gaps with runtime truth rather than more inference, using\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-80-two native-image flags:\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-81-\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-82-- `--exact-reachability-metadata` makes the native image treat any access that\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-83-  is **not** backed by supplied metadata as a hard miss instead of silently\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md:84:  registering it. With `-H:MissingRegistrationReportingMode=Exit`, the binary\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-85-  exits `ExitStatus.MISSING_METADATA` (172) and prints the exact missing entry\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-86-  the instant it hits an unregistered access.\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-87-- The same `runNativeTraceImage` execution that detects the miss also records\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-88-  it: the missing entry is written into that cycle's trace directory as a\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-89-  ground-truth metadata entry (§WF-native-trace-gradle-tasks). Feeding that\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-90-  directory back through `metadataConfigDirs` makes the next build aware of the\n--\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-115-### WF-native-tracing-reporter-divergence: Reporter and tracer are separate components\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-116-\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-117-Under the tracing build flags (§WF-native-trace-gradle-tasks), two\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-118-*independent* GraalVM Native Image components cooperate on each\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-119-`runNativeTraceImage` cycle:\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-120-\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md:121:- the **missing-registration reporter** (`--exact-reachability-metadata`,\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md:122:  `-H:MissingRegistrationReportingMode=Exit`) detects an access that is not\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-123-  backed by supplied metadata, prints the exact missing entry, and exits the\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-124-  binary with `ExitStatus.MISSING_METADATA` (172);\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-125-- the **metadata tracer** (`-H:+MetadataTracingSupport`) writes the accesses the\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-126-  execution observes into the trace directory named by `-PtraceMetadataPath`.\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-127-\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-128-**Invariant.** Every entry the reporter prints as missing in a cycle must be\n--\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-235-  `user-code-filter.json` when available. Maven groups are often not Java\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-236-  package roots (for example an `org.apache.tomcat.embed` artifact can execute\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-237-  `org.apache.catalina`, `org.apache.coyote`, and `org.apache.tomcat` code).\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-238-  Using the package filter keeps tracing able to select a condition class that\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-239-  is actually on the access stack before a missing metadata access occurs. If\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-240-  the filter cannot be read, the legacy `[group]` fallback is used.\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md:241:- **Inactive metadata conditions are too-late conditions.** When GraalVM reports\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md:242:  that metadata for an access exists but is inactive because runtime conditions\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-243-  were not satisfied, the repair must move or duplicate the matching metadata\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-244-  under a condition reached before the access. The condition should be inferred\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-245-  from the access stack, usually the library frame performing the reflective,\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-246-  resource, proxy, serialization, or JNI access. Reusing the unsatisfied\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-247-  condition is invalid because it preserves the same timing failure.\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-248-- **Native test run second.** After JVM-agent metadata is generated, the\n--\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-270-  -PtraceMetadataConditionPackages=<packages>\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-271-  -PmetadataConfigDirs=<config_dirs>` where `config_dirs` is the staged\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-272-  agent dir, when present, followed by accepted trace dirs. The last\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-273-  property is omitted only when no staged agent metadata and no accepted\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-274-  trace dirs exist. The resulting binary is built with `-H:+MetadataTracingSupport`,\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-275-  `--exact-reachability-metadata`, and\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md:276:  `-H:MissingRegistrationReportingMode=Exit` (see the `runNativeTraceImage`\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-277-  contract, §WF-native-trace-gradle-tasks).\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-278-  The same execution writes a trace dir **and** returns an\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-279-  exact-metadata-aware exit code.\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-280-- **Exit-code routing**:\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-281-  - `0` → the metadata accumulated in `config_dirs` plus the code under\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-282-    test are sufficient. The gate runs `mergeNativeTraceMetadata` to\n--\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-383-Build-flag behavior:\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-384-\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-385-- The task adds `-H:+UnlockExperimentalVMOptions\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-386-  -H:+MetadataTracingSupport -H:-UnlockExperimentalVMOptions` so the binary's\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-387-  **tracer** writes traced metadata at runtime.\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-388-- The task **also** adds `--exact-reachability-metadata` and\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md:389:  `-H:MissingRegistrationReportingMode=Exit`. These make the **reporter** exit\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-390-  the binary with `ExitStatus.MISSING_METADATA` (172) when an access misses the\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-391-  metadata supplied via `-PmetadataConfigDirs`, instead of throwing. The gate\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-392-  routes on this exit code (§WF-native-test-verification-gate).\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-393-\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-394-Runtime behavior:\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-395-\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-396-- The task always invokes the binary the same way. There are no\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-397-  caller-supplied program arguments.\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-398-- **The tracer must record whatever the reporter reports missing.** When the\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md:399:  missing-registration reporter prints a missing dynamic-access entry to\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-400-  stdout/stderr, the same `runNativeTraceImage` invocation must add the\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-401-  equivalent entry to the trace directory passed by `-PtraceMetadataPath`. The\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-402-  metadata kind, condition package, and target identity reported to the user\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-403-  must match the entry later consumed by `mergeNativeTraceMetadata`; otherwise\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-404-  the trace loop has not produced a trustworthy runtime-observed signal. A\n./forge/docs/workflows/native-metadata-tracing.md-405-  reporter/tracer divergence here is a Native Image defect and is handled per\n--\n./COVERAGE.md-1050-| `org.aspectj:aspectjrt` | [1.9.6<br>- 1.9.25](metadata/org.aspectj/aspectjrt/index.json) | <details><summary>Show</summary> AspectJ is an aspect-oriented extension to Java, and aspectjrt provides the runtime APIs, annotations, join point types, and reflection support needed by woven AspectJ code. Applications use it at runtime to execute aspects compiled or woven with AspectJ without bundling the compiler or weaver.</details> | [100.0% (72/72 calls)](stats/org.aspectj/aspectjrt/) |\n./COVERAGE.md-1051-| `org.aspectj:aspectjweaver` | [1.9.7<br>- 1.9.20](metadata/org.aspectj/aspectjweaver/index.json) | <details><summary>Show</summary> AspectJ Weaver applies AspectJ aspects to Java classes at compile time, post-compile time, or load time. The artifact can run as a Java agent for load-time weaving and includes the runtime classes needed by woven AspectJ code.</details> | [99.4% (155/156 calls)](stats/org.aspectj/aspectjweaver/) |\n./COVERAGE.md-1052-| `org.asynchttpclient:async-http-client` | [2.12.3<br>- 3.0.11](metadata/org.asynchttpclient/async-http-client/index.json) | <details><summary>Show</summary> Async Http Client is a Java library for 